(5448236, 782056, 70128, '<td valign="top">First of all, thanks to all the commenters!<br/> <br/>ProdigalMedic: this was post process sepia. This train is a museum now, and it has a horrible pink sticker band keeping doors from being opened, that''s why I had to either use black &amp; white or sepia, to hide it as much as possible.<br/> <br/>smudgeSMJ: I tried it in B&amp;W too, but I found it too "busy". It was hard to tell what it was. Sepia gave it some more contrast and depth.<br/> <br/>Teafran: thank you so very much for your comments. They are always very nice and constructive. I really appreciate the time you take to give your point of view!</td>', 'First of all, thanks to all the commenters! ProdigalMedic: this was post process sepia. This train is a museum now, and it has a horrible pink sticker band keeping doors from being opened, that''s why I had to either use black & white or sepia, to hide it as much as possible. smudgeSMJ: I tried it in B&W too, but I found it too "busy". It was hard to tell what it was. Sepia gave it some more contrast and depth. Teafran: thank you so very much for your comments. They are always very nice and constructive. I really appreciate the time you take to give your point of view!', '2009-04-22 09:18:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448244, 780758, 91496, '<td valign="top">Nice find. I really like the colors, DOF, and the unique viewpoint.  I think the centered composition with the red light almost dead center may have knocked it down a little in the scoring.  A squarish crop of the right hand side seems a strong composition.  Also trying to put the red light on the thirds in csmera and keeping the retangular crop may have looked cool as well.</td>', 'Nice find. I really like the colors, DOF, and the unique viewpoint.  I think the centered composition with the red light almost dead center may have knocked it down a little in the scoring.  A squarish crop of the right hand side seems a strong composition.  Also trying to put the red light on the thirds in csmera and keeping the retangular crop may have looked cool as well.', '2009-04-22 09:26:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448250, 781852, 73235, '<td valign="top">WOW, congratulations for a great picture and a PB and breaking the 6! Well done!</td>', 'WOW, congratulations for a great picture and a PB and breaking the 6! Well done!', '2009-04-22 09:31:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448251, 781964, 86359, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the nice picture and first ribbon!Also blue!</td>', 'Congrats on the nice picture and first ribbon!Also blue!', '2009-04-22 09:31:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448254, 781160, 81530, '<td valign="top">Good Finish Buddy :)</td>', 'Good Finish Buddy :)', '2009-04-22 09:35:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448256, 781974, 40386, '<td valign="top">I knew this had to be yours as soon as I saw it, congrats on your top 10, it is truly a great opportunity that I hope you will exploit often, each one has its own unique appeal.</td>', 'I knew this had to be yours as soon as I saw it, congrats on your top 10, it is truly a great opportunity that I hope you will exploit often, each one has its own unique appeal.', '2009-04-22 09:37:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448273, 782420, 54645, '<td valign="top">I like the Bert ''O9 scrawled in the soot and the classic train composition. I also like the halo in this image, it''s an artifact that created a vignette! Looks decent to me. I do agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=101256" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">teafran</a>''s comment below about the sharpening artifacts throughout the image. Congrats on your ribbon, it matches the engine!</td>', 'I like the Bert ''O9 scrawled in the soot and the classic train composition. I also like the halo in this image, it''s an artifact that created a vignette! Looks decent to me. I do agree with  teafran''s comment below about the sharpening artifacts throughout the image. Congrats on your ribbon, it matches the engine!', '2009-04-22 09:48:21.000000', NULL, 0),
