(5448390, 782024, 54212, '<td valign="top">Interesting comments. After waiting all week for the sun to come out (it didn''t), finally had to just take a picture (or actually lots - 100+). Photo taken at high noon on a very cloudy day, extremely flat light. Early AM and late PM lighting sucked too, just darker. Any adjustments didn''t do much and early spring in N. MN has no color.</td>', 'Interesting comments. After waiting all week for the sun to come out (it didn''t), finally had to just take a picture (or actually lots - 100+). Photo taken at high noon on a very cloudy day, extremely flat light. Early AM and late PM lighting sucked too, just darker. Any adjustments didn''t do much and early spring in N. MN has no color.', '2009-04-22 11:15:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448392, 782334, 30861, '<td valign="top">Managed real well, didn''t ya? Congrats!</td>', 'Managed real well, didn''t ya? Congrats!', '2009-04-22 11:16:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448426, 782321, 48954, '<td valign="top">What could have you done to improve this shot? Well my opinion is that this is nothing special. Taking into consideration what type of photography wins on this site this is a photo not "worth" remembering. It doesn''t stand out. It''s just a picture of a train standing. As others have mentioned, crisp, clear and good composition but very interesting. "Anyone" could have taken the shot if you know what I mean.</td>', 'What could have you done to improve this shot? Well my opinion is that this is nothing special. Taking into consideration what type of photography wins on this site this is a photo not "worth" remembering. It doesn''t stand out. It''s just a picture of a train standing. As others have mentioned, crisp, clear and good composition but very interesting. "Anyone" could have taken the shot if you know what I mean.', '2009-04-22 11:48:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448436, 781852, 46778, '<td valign="top">Choo Choo into your first 6+. Congrats for a great finish, personal best and very nice picture.</td>', 'Choo Choo into your first 6+. Congrats for a great finish, personal best and very nice picture.', '2009-04-22 12:00:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448443, 782420, 39057, '<td valign="top">Very nice. The only way I could see this being done in Basic is with the use of the "highlights/shadows" tool. However, I could never get this nice effect throughout the photo with H/S only. I have to use the burn/dodge brush. I get sections of altered highlights and sections of altered shadows...it usually looks bad.<br/> <br/>Clarify in PS Pro is also mentioned. Did you use PSP exclusivly for this shot?<br/> <br/>If you don''t mind, can you post your steps on this shot in DP or do a Youtube tutorial?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-22 11:08:44.</i></td>', 'Very nice. The only way I could see this being done in Basic is with the use of the "highlights/shadows" tool. However, I could never get this nice effect throughout the photo with H/S only. I have to use the burn/dodge brush. I get sections of altered highlights and sections of altered shadows...it usually looks bad. Clarify in PS Pro is also mentioned. Did you use PSP exclusivly for this shot? If you don''t mind, can you post your steps on this shot in DP or do a Youtube tutorial?', '2009-04-22 12:07:40.000000', '2009-04-22 12:08:44.000000', 0),
(5448472, 781723, 57229, '<td valign="top">Why do you call it ''railroad'' instead of ''railway''? Indeed, if it were really GWR, wouldn''t it have a 7'' wheelspan? Come to think of it, maybe the chassis is sort of overhanging the wheels by 1''2" either side...<br/> <br/>Can somebody hold this anorak for a minute?<br/> <br/>Lovely picture, congrats on the ribbon.</td>', 'Why do you call it ''railroad'' instead of ''railway''? Indeed, if it were really GWR, wouldn''t it have a 7'' wheelspan? Come to think of it, maybe the chassis is sort of overhanging the wheels by 1''2" either side... Can somebody hold this anorak for a minute? Lovely picture, congrats on the ribbon.', '2009-04-22 12:21:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448568, 782420, 102315, '<td valign="top">I am still interested In knowig how this was done. As per your pre challenge comments this looks like an HDR. Especially with the halo effect that was created.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-22 17:23:09.</i></td>', 'I am still interested In knowig how this was done. As per your pre challenge comments this looks like an HDR. Especially with the halo effect that was created.', '2009-04-22 13:30:59.000000', '2009-04-22 18:23:09.000000', 0),
(5448577, 781964, 49109, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your well deserved blue, great shot!</td>', 'Congrats on your well deserved blue, great shot!', '2009-04-22 13:34:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448583, 782321, 58457, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smyk:</b></div><hr/><i> What could have you done to improve this shot? Well my opinion is that this is nothing special. Taking into consideration what type of photography wins on this site this is a photo not "worth" remembering. It doesn''t stand out. It''s just a picture of a train standing. As others have mentioned, crisp, clear and good composition but very interesting. "Anyone" could have taken the shot if you know what I mean. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree w/ this comment (saw your request thread).  Its just nothing special.  Is it in focus, yes.  Exposed correctly, yes.  Does it get me any other response... not really.  I probably would have given it a 5.  Maybe cranking up the contrast.  Perhaps a wide angle view taken from lower and closer to the train to exaggerate its size.  Maybe taken at sunsets so there is detail or clouds in the sky.  Try it again if you can on a different day.  Go an hour before sunset and see how many different pictures you can take--maybe you''ll find a winner.  I struggle with subjects like these myself--its tough to make the mundane and normal interesting.</td>', 'Originally posted by smyk: What could have you done to improve this shot? Well my opinion is that this is nothing special. Taking into consideration what type of photography wins on this site this is a photo not "worth" remembering. It doesn''t stand out. It''s just a picture of a train standing. As others have mentioned, crisp, clear and good composition but very interesting. "Anyone" could have taken the shot if you know what I mean.   I agree w/ this comment (saw your request thread).  Its just nothing special.  Is it in focus, yes.  Exposed correctly, yes.  Does it get me any other response... not really.  I probably would have given it a 5.  Maybe cranking up the contrast.  Perhaps a wide angle view taken from lower and closer to the train to exaggerate its size.  Maybe taken at sunsets so there is detail or clouds in the sky.  Try it again if you can on a different day.  Go an hour before sunset and see how many different pictures you can take--maybe you''ll find a winner.  I struggle with subjects like these myself--its tough to make the mundane and normal interesting.', '2009-04-22 13:36:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448696, 782222, 103411, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 7, I think the voters were too unkind here.</td>', 'I gave you a 7, I think the voters were too unkind here.', '2009-04-22 14:53:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448699, 782351, 103411, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 7, I think the voters were too unkind here... doesn''t fit the high score mold I guess.</td>', 'I gave you a 7, I think the voters were too unkind here... doesn''t fit the high score mold I guess.', '2009-04-22 14:55:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448708, 782321, 36470, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smyk:</b></div><hr/><i> What could have you done to improve this shot? Well my opinion is that this is nothing special. Taking into consideration what type of photography wins on this site this is a photo not "worth" remembering. It doesn''t stand out. It''s just a picture of a train standing. As others have mentioned, crisp, clear and good composition but very interesting. "Anyone" could have taken the shot if you know what I mean. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I''d have to agree here.  Sometimes the technicals of the pic can be done well, but if the subject doesn''t jump out and bite you, the score will reflect that.</td>', 'Originally posted by smyk: What could have you done to improve this shot? Well my opinion is that this is nothing special. Taking into consideration what type of photography wins on this site this is a photo not "worth" remembering. It doesn''t stand out. It''s just a picture of a train standing. As others have mentioned, crisp, clear and good composition but very interesting. "Anyone" could have taken the shot if you know what I mean.   I''d have to agree here.  Sometimes the technicals of the pic can be done well, but if the subject doesn''t jump out and bite you, the score will reflect that.', '2009-04-22 15:01:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5448728, 782321, 6519, '<td valign="top">We are spoiled rotten these days.<br/>A technically fine photo of a fine subject just doesn''t do it anymore.<br/>We get to see sooooooo many of those, that we need something special and different to make us look twice and vote higher.<br/> <br/>There is nothing wrong with your photo at all, it just lacks that something extra.</td>', 'We are spoiled rotten these days.A technically fine photo of a fine subject just doesn''t do it anymore.We get to see sooooooo many of those, that we need something special and different to make us look twice and vote higher. There is nothing wrong with your photo at all, it just lacks that something extra.', '2009-04-22 15:16:09.000000', NULL, 0),
