(5449530, 782205, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677021" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677021.jpg"/></a> PostLuminous Nominee<br/>there ya go again--another marvelous station shot and luminous conversion!</td>', ' PostLuminous Nomineethere ya go again--another marvelous station shot and luminous conversion!', '2009-04-23 00:20:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449549, 781177, 82985, '<td valign="top"><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=677020" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/80000-84999/82985/120/677020.jpg"/></a> Postluminous Winner!<br/> <br/>simple, direct, sublime...</td>', ' Postluminous Winner! simple, direct, sublime...', '2009-04-23 00:34:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449662, 781384, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Criticque Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: As mentioned in my earlier comment, I love these old trains and I like the sepia. I find this shot to be very atmospheric and evocative of the time that these trains ran the rails. <br/> <br/>Technical: I like the composition here as it helps show off the immensity and solidity of the engine.  Good dof and I am a fan of this kind of pov.  Looks like it was shot on a slightly overcast day as there aren''t any telltale areas of glare on the metal.  Light in upper left borders on being flat, but isn''t, so good that there is a softness there to contrast with the engine.<br/> <br/>Artistic: Very good choice of pof, but the crop is a bit tight.  I''d like to see more room in front of the train, so there is a sense of a place for it to go.  Also, would like to see either the top of the cab, or all of the wheels, just to further enhance the scale.<br/> <br/>The pp is quite pleasing, and very clever idea to use the sepia tint to help hide the Christmas lights! One trick I learned here on dpc is to do all your image adjustment work first, then resize, usm, and save for web.<br/> <br/>All in all, still very much one of my favourite shots from that challenge, and I am glad I got the chance to criticque it.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me any questions you may have.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Criticque Club! Initial impression: As mentioned in my earlier comment, I love these old trains and I like the sepia. I find this shot to be very atmospheric and evocative of the time that these trains ran the rails.  Technical: I like the composition here as it helps show off the immensity and solidity of the engine.  Good dof and I am a fan of this kind of pov.  Looks like it was shot on a slightly overcast day as there aren''t any telltale areas of glare on the metal.  Light in upper left borders on being flat, but isn''t, so good that there is a softness there to contrast with the engine. Artistic: Very good choice of pof, but the crop is a bit tight.  I''d like to see more room in front of the train, so there is a sense of a place for it to go.  Also, would like to see either the top of the cab, or all of the wheels, just to further enhance the scale. The pp is quite pleasing, and very clever idea to use the sepia tint to help hide the Christmas lights! One trick I learned here on dpc is to do all your image adjustment work first, then resize, usm, and save for web. All in all, still very much one of my favourite shots from that challenge, and I am glad I got the chance to criticque it. Feel free to PM me any questions you may have. Susan', '2009-04-23 02:24:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449723, 781964, 103916, '<td valign="top">I love this picture.  You captured both, emotion and mystery in this photograph in such a wonderful photograph.  Congratulations on your first ribbon.  You deserve it dear....Be proud of your accomplishment, you did a fantastic job!!!!</td>', 'I love this picture.  You captured both, emotion and mystery in this photograph in such a wonderful photograph.  Congratulations on your first ribbon.  You deserve it dear....Be proud of your accomplishment, you did a fantastic job!!!!', '2009-04-23 06:32:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449724, 781723, 103916, '<td valign="top">Fantastic Job!!!  Great photograph!  To me, it seems to be a photograph that you can just gaze upon for sometime and still find more reasons why this photograph is so great.  =)</td>', 'Fantastic Job!!!  Great photograph!  To me, it seems to be a photograph that you can just gaze upon for sometime and still find more reasons why this photograph is so great.  =)', '2009-04-23 06:36:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449859, 782338, 70270, '<td valign="top">I like the tight crop -- its a bit different for this challenge, and worked well, particularly with the shallow DOF you used.  My only nit is the headlamp cut down the middle.  Shows a nice bit of detail of your train, and colors and sharpness are spot on.</td>', 'I like the tight crop -- its a bit different for this challenge, and worked well, particularly with the shallow DOF you used.  My only nit is the headlamp cut down the middle.  Shows a nice bit of detail of your train, and colors and sharpness are spot on.', '2009-04-23 10:36:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449865, 781536, 70270, '<td valign="top">I liked how you composed this, the wide expanse of the land and the lonely engine off to the side, seeming abandoned as the ragged bushes grew up around it in the middle of nowhere, or so it seems.  Nicely seen scene that should have done better in the challenge.</td>', 'I liked how you composed this, the wide expanse of the land and the lonely engine off to the side, seeming abandoned as the ragged bushes grew up around it in the middle of nowhere, or so it seems.  Nicely seen scene that should have done better in the challenge.', '2009-04-23 10:41:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449871, 782350, 70270, '<td valign="top">Nicely different composition and scene.  I like how you kept the one spike anchoring the frame in the lower left, and just enough of the station to give us context to follow the line back up the track.  The off kilter frame works for me, only nit is I it could use just a tad more sharpness on the foreground rail, perhaps by shooting at f/16 or smaller rather than 5.6.</td>', 'Nicely different composition and scene.  I like how you kept the one spike anchoring the frame in the lower left, and just enough of the station to give us context to follow the line back up the track.  The off kilter frame works for me, only nit is I it could use just a tad more sharpness on the foreground rail, perhaps by shooting at f/16 or smaller rather than 5.6.', '2009-04-23 10:45:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449877, 781384, 70270, '<td valign="top">What a great old engine, and the color treatment worked well to hide the lights ... I kept looking and looking to see if I could find them and I couldn''t!  Great subject, though I think this would have worked a bit better if you would have either chosen to go in much closer to focus in on some of the detail and the shapes and forms of the engine rather than the whole thing, or stepped back a bit farther to show us the whole engine and some of its surroundings.</td>', 'What a great old engine, and the color treatment worked well to hide the lights ... I kept looking and looking to see if I could find them and I couldn''t!  Great subject, though I think this would have worked a bit better if you would have either chosen to go in much closer to focus in on some of the detail and the shapes and forms of the engine rather than the whole thing, or stepped back a bit farther to show us the whole engine and some of its surroundings.', '2009-04-23 10:55:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449919, 782342, 103309, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by bvy:</b></div><hr/><i> This is excellent! Love those lines, great contrast and black and white. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you so much!</td>', 'Originally posted by bvy: This is excellent! Love those lines, great contrast and black and white.   Thank you so much!', '2009-04-23 12:03:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449922, 782342, 103309, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Teafran:</b></div><hr/><i> Crisp and sharp which is a major plus - a good grayscale.  Lots of details, good angle which shows off the linear nature of the times and roof, but keeping the curving sweep into the distance. The author took time to do the best job in difficult lighting as the highlights are right on the edge of being over done. Unfortunately, it could have used some more "action" and if the author had taken a little more time to catch a sense of speed with the oncoming train, along with reducing the foreground tile flares, it would have been perfect. Well done. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you for the detailed comment...much appreciated!<br/>What kills me is it was a toss up between two shots. The other (which I was leaning towards) had more of the train coming through (good action) but I had trouble uploading it. <br/>Thanks again</td>', 'Originally posted by Teafran: Crisp and sharp which is a major plus - a good grayscale.  Lots of details, good angle which shows off the linear nature of the times and roof, but keeping the curving sweep into the distance. The author took time to do the best job in difficult lighting as the highlights are right on the edge of being over done. Unfortunately, it could have used some more "action" and if the author had taken a little more time to catch a sense of speed with the oncoming train, along with reducing the foreground tile flares, it would have been perfect. Well done.   Thank you for the detailed comment...much appreciated!What kills me is it was a toss up between two shots. The other (which I was leaning towards) had more of the train coming through (good action) but I had trouble uploading it. Thanks again', '2009-04-23 12:05:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449928, 781542, 66384, '<td valign="top">Terrific angle and beautiful color. I really like it. Congratulations on the good score and placement.</td>', 'Terrific angle and beautiful color. I really like it. Congratulations on the good score and placement.', '2009-04-23 12:17:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449984, 782420, 60495, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rugman1969:</b></div><hr/><i> Basic editing rules:<br/> <br/>You may not:<br/> <br/>spot-edit your entry, except to remove sensor dust or hot pixels<br/> <br/>use any selection tool, including but not limited to the marquee, lasso, layer masks, quick masks, or any similar tool to select a portion of your image for any reason other than cropping or creating a border. <br/> <br/>use ANY editing tool to create new image area, objects or features (such as <b>VIGNETTES</b>, lens flare or motion) that didnt already exist in your original capture.<br/> <br/>An entry will be disqualified when a majority of the Site Council finds that <b>ANY</b> of the rules above were not followed. <br/> <br/>The above penalties will be assessed only after review by the Site Council. In exceptional circumstances, the Site Council may elect not to apply a penalty. <b>If a user is found to have intentionally violated the Challenge Rules,</b> the above penalties will be in addition to any assessed for the violation itself. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The key wording is <b><u>if</u></b>,  Tom mentioned the shot has been validated so the <u><b>if</b></u> portion is no longer a question. Just because you can not accomplish this effect does not make it illegal. Why is it so hard to congratulate someone and trust they were within the rules until SC makes the call!<br/> <br/>Again great job Tom!</td>', 'Originally posted by rugman1969: Basic editing rules: You may not: spot-edit your entry, except to remove sensor dust or hot pixels use any selection tool, including but not limited to the marquee, lasso, layer masks, quick masks, or any similar tool to select a portion of your image for any reason other than cropping or creating a border.  use ANY editing tool to create new image area, objects or features (such as VIGNETTES, lens flare or motion) that didnt already exist in your original capture. An entry will be disqualified when a majority of the Site Council finds that ANY of the rules above were not followed.  The above penalties will be assessed only after review by the Site Council. In exceptional circumstances, the Site Council may elect not to apply a penalty. If a user is found to have intentionally violated the Challenge Rules, the above penalties will be in addition to any assessed for the violation itself.   The key wording is if,  Tom mentioned the shot has been validated so the if portion is no longer a question. Just because you can not accomplish this effect does not make it illegal. Why is it so hard to congratulate someone and trust they were within the rules until SC makes the call! Again great job Tom!', '2009-04-23 13:55:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449993, 781964, 24454, '<td valign="top">This is SO AMAZING!  I love train photos anyway -- but this one has all the glam and drama that definitely make it a blue ribbon winner!  Congratulations!</td>', 'This is SO AMAZING!  I love train photos anyway -- but this one has all the glam and drama that definitely make it a blue ribbon winner!  Congratulations!', '2009-04-23 14:14:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(5449997, 781723, 24454, '<td valign="top">The crop doesn''t look strange to me at all.   I have always been a fan of square crops.  The pictures look so much bigger and larger than life when they are square.   This is amazing.  I''m so glad you had a great day, and a ribbon to put the icing on the cake -- or I should say the memory :)   Congratulations MAK!  You continue to be AWESOME! :)<br/></td>', 'The crop doesn''t look strange to me at all.   I have always been a fan of square crops.  The pictures look so much bigger and larger than life when they are square.   This is amazing.  I''m so glad you had a great day, and a ribbon to put the icing on the cake -- or I should say the memory :)   Congratulations MAK!  You continue to be AWESOME! :)', '2009-04-23 14:17:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(5450015, 782420, 24454, '<td valign="top">Verrrry nice!  Now you got me curious tho about the reaction from a few commenters. . .better go check it out:<br/> <br/>Oyyyyyy. .. some people spend way too much time looking for things to get their tail feathers in a ruffle about instead of just enjoying great photography!<br/> <br/>WAY TO GO on capturing an amazing photo -- processed to perfection -- and on getting the last word!!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Verrrry nice!  Now you got me curious tho about the reaction from a few commenters. . .better go check it out: Oyyyyyy. .. some people spend way too much time looking for things to get their tail feathers in a ruffle about instead of just enjoying great photography! WAY TO GO on capturing an amazing photo -- processed to perfection -- and on getting the last word!!! ', '2009-04-23 14:31:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(5450105, 782223, 24454, '<td valign="top">I love it!   I''m sure glad you did.   This is the kind of train photo, with all the smoke and dusky light that really grabs me.  Congratulations on an honorable mention!</td>', 'I love it!   I''m sure glad you did.   This is the kind of train photo, with all the smoke and dusky light that really grabs me.  Congratulations on an honorable mention!', '2009-04-23 16:32:44.000000', NULL, 0),
